1. What you may do

   a) Read, study and build this source code on your own computers.
   b) Use a copy you built yourself for personal, non-commercial purposes. The free
      features are free. The paid features (Pro and Ultimate) are for use with a valid
      key bought from the project, or a free promo key it issued.
   c) Contribute improvements: fork the repository on GitHub to send a pull request,
      report issues, and discuss it.

2. What you may not do

   a) Sell, rent, sublicense or distribute the software, or any copy, build, app,
      installer or derivative of it, in source or binary form, or publish a fork as a
      product people can run, without written permission from the copyright holder.
   b) Use the software or its code commercially, in a product or a service.
   c) Remove, bypass, disable or change the licence, activation, entitlement, update,
      revocation or tier checks, or unlock Pro or Ultimate features without a valid key;
      or make, share or sell keys, key generators, cracks, patches or tools that do.
   d) Attack, overload or probe the project's servers, or use them other than through
      an unmodified official build in the ordinary way. Report security problems
      privately to the copyright holder instead.
   e) Use the name "Notch apple", its icon or its logo in a way that suggests your
      version is official or endorsed.

